<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST476"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, July 14, 2004 - 8:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->06/09/75 - Carol Marstellar, 32 yo Wichita woman found in a ditch northeast of Wichita. She had been stabbed may times to the abdomen. She had also been beatem in the head and chest by possible the knife handle. She was last seen about 11:30 pm Wednesday leaving the Brookside Club at , &#40;get this address&#41; 717 S. Market Roomate was Katherine Long, who last saw her. <BR> <BR>The body lay face up amoung weeds. The left hand lay across the woman&#39;s midsection. <BR> <BR>Jaden<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 476-->
<!--Post: 602--><!--Time: 1090897525-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST602"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 8:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This sounds like a &#34;personal cause&#34; homicide but a few things indicate she may have been a BTK victim.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 602-->
<!--Post: 1151--><!--Time: 1097455608-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1151"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Quell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Quell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, October 10, 2004 - 5:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have read elsewhere that serial killers very much do pose their victims.  This posing situation would match the Wegerle photo.  BTK without a doubt.  Sexual serial killers gravitate toward mutilation/maiming as well as placing foreign objects in the victims&#39; sexual areas.  Was there anything found on ANY of these victims?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1151-->
<!--Post: 8502--><!--Time: 1109178907-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8502"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 9:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->G <BR>   There are some curious coincidences here.  <BR>   VERY curious. <BR> <BR>Let’s look at David G. Packard: <BR> <BR>    He was born in 1950, and is 6&#39;2&#34; tall with light brown hair.  <BR>   <BR>    Carol Martstellar was killed June 5, 1975.  On July 14, 1986 David G. Packard was arrested and charged with her murder in Sedgwick County district court case 86CR774.  <BR> <BR>    At the time of his arrest, he was employed by East Tulsa Office Supply. [copiers ?] <BR> <BR>    Packard posted bond on July 31, 1986.  He was required to stay in Tulsa County Oklahoma and call the Tulsa Co Sheriff nightly at 6:00pm.  He could not leave Tulsa Co. except for court or to visit his lawyer in Wichita. <BR>   <BR>     He had required court appearances on August 6th 1986 and September 29th 1986, and would have been meeting with his lawyer during the time of the Wegerly homicide September 13th 1986. <BR>   <BR>     His lawyer&#39;s office was in the 1400 block of north Broadway, 1.98 miles from the Wegerly home. <BR> <BR>     The Wegerly home is on 13th street, which is a direct route between the lawyer’s office and Hwy 235, which links to I-35 to Oklahoma.  <BR> <BR>     Packard had to use direct routes to comply with his bond conditions. <BR> <BR>     Mr. Wegerly&#39;s sister was a Sedgwick County court reporter who worked on the floor where Packard&#39;s preliminary hearing was held on August 6th 1986. <BR> <BR>     Packard was convicted and taken into custody on Mar 25, 1987.  Kansas Department of Correction records show that he spent 18 years in Lansing penitentiary, until he reported to his parole officer in Oklahoma on Mar 23, 2004. He was released on parole in Kansas earlier and then transferred to Oklahoma.  He was out of prison March 19th 2004. <BR> <BR>     There were no BTK communications or killings while Packard was in prison. <BR> <BR>     Packard gave a DNA sample when he was placed on parole, but the backlog is so massive that it probably hasn&#39;t been tested.   <BR> <BR>     Link to news article about the parole hearing: <a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/515277.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/515277.html</a> <BR> <BR>     Link to parole website for Packard with photo: <a href="http://www.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/offender.asp?id=15497" target=_top>http://www.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/offender.asp?id= 15497</a> <BR> <BR>    Hmmmmmmmmmmm….. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8502-->
