<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8599"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 9:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fascinating, Who!  But was he out on March 17, when the March 19 2004 letter was postmarked?  Or is there another explanation for the mailing time?  I just want to see in black and white when he was out the door and on the street in order to get to a Wichita mailbox on March 17.  Thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
