<!--Post: 8618--><!--Time: 1109252510-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8618"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->His first communication was received on March 19th and post marked March 17th 2004. I say he is very interesting, but the dates of the first confirmed communication do not match. The first communication contained Vickie Weargerle&#39;s drivers license and photo&#39;s of the crime scene that were apparently taken by the killer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
