<!--Post: 8624--><!--Time: 1109254090-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8624"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 6:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tops, <BR>I just called the Kansas Parole Department I want to know if there might be a window from release date to parole date since he transferred out of state.  <BR> <BR>I will have to wait 2 hours due to the time difference their office opens at 8 am.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8624-->
<!--Post: 8628--><!--Time: 1109255004-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8628"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 6:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great Blade! Hopefully we can get a precise answer. Because they clearly clearly state twice that his movement date and release date is the 23rd of March. I coudnt understand where whoisbtk was getting that he was out on the 19th. I have tried to find any information that supports it but so far have not. He would be a prime POI if this can be supported.  <BR> <BR>Kind of off topic-why in hell is this guy on parole??? I know his family proclaims he is innocent but he was tried and convicted! If his family only <i>knew</i> how many inmates &#34;didnt do it!&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
